Pumpkin Muffins
  --John Kanell

1 1/2 c ap flour (180g)
2 1/2 tsp pumpkin pie spice
1 tsp baking soda
1/2 tsp baking powder
1/2 tsp salt
1/2 c packed light brown sugar (110g)
1/2 c sugar (100g)
1/2 c vegetable oil (120mL)
1/4 c whole milk room temperature (60mL)
2 large eggs room
1 tsp vanilla extract
1 1/4 c canned pumpkin puree

Preheat the oven to 425F. Line a muffin pan with 12 paper liners. In a large bowl, combine the flour, spices, baking powder, baking soda, and salt, then whisk together until combined. In a medium bowl, whisk together the sugars, oil, milk, eggs, and vanilla until well combined. Add in the pumpkin puree and whisk until smooth. Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients and mix together using a silicone spatula until just combined and no dry streaks of flour remain. Divide the batter among the paper liners, filling each one ~3/4 full. Bake for 5 min at 425F. Without opening the oven, reduce the oven temperature to 350F, and bake for an additional 15 min or until a wooden pick inserted in the center comes out clean. Remove the muffins from the pan and let them cool completely on a wire rack.


Notes: can use any milk, or water if you don't have milk. can add 2/3 c choc chips or nuts. can add streusel or glaze to top
